MUSE 2 SETUP
============

Windows
-------
Use BlueMuse: https://github.com/kowalej/BlueMuse
  1. Install from Microsoft Store or the GitHub releases page.
  2. Pair the Muse 2 via Windows Bluetooth settings.
  3. Open BlueMuse, find the device, click "Start LSL".
  4. Confirm the EEG stream appears in LabRecorder before starting the experiment.

macOS / Linux
-------------
Use muselsl: https://github.com/alexandrebarachant/muse-lsl
  pip install muselsl

  Option A — manual (recommended for first-time setup):
    muselsl stream          # in a dedicated terminal, leave it running

  Option B — automatic (via run_experiment.py):
    python run_experiment.py --start-muselsl

Stream details (Muse 2)
-----------------------
  Channels    : 4 EEG (TP9, AF7, AF8, TP10) + accelerometer + gyroscope
  Sample rate : ~256 Hz
  LSL type    : 'EEG'
  BlueMuse also provides a 'Telemetry' stream (battery, Horse Shoe quality).

Signal quality check
--------------------
  Watch the Horse Shoe indicator in BlueMuse (Windows) or the terminal output
  from muselsl before placing the headset on the participant. All four nodes
  should show green/good contact before starting LabRecorder.
